{"id":"tradition","lemma":"Tradition","pos":"noun","rank":2562,"glosses":["tradition"],"ipa":"/tʁadiˈt͡si̯oːn/","audio":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/c/c0/De-Tradition.ogg/De-Tradition.ogg.mp3","gender":"f","forms":{"genitive":"Tradition","plural":"Traditionen"},"examples":[{"text":"Du verstehst unsere Traditionen gut.","en":"You understand our traditions well.","words":[{"g":"you"},{"g":"to hear and interpret","l":"verstehen"},{"g":"our","l":"unser"},null,{"g":"good"}]},{"text":"Das ist eine alte Tradition.","en":"It's a time-honored tradition.","words":[{"g":"the / that"},{"g":"is","l":"sein"},{"g":"a"},{"g":"age, old age","l":"Alter"},null]},{"text":"Gute Traditionen sollte man erhalten.","en":"Good traditions should be preserved.","words":[{"g":"good","l":"gut"},null,{"g":"should","l":"sollen"},{"g":"one"},{"g":"to receive"}]},{"text":"Einige Traditionen werden sich nie ändern.","en":"Some customs will never change.","words":[{"g":"united","l":"einig"},null,{"g":"to become"},{"g":"oneself"},{"g":"never, never at all"},{"g":"to change, to alter"}]},{"text":"Er kehrte der alten Tradition den Rücken zu.","en":"He turned his back on the old tradition.","words":[{"g":"he / it"},{"g":"to turn","l":"kehren"},{"g":"the"},{"g":"old","l":"alt"},null,{"g":"the","l":"der"},{"g":"back"},{"g":"to / too"}]}]}